// The write-after-read policy AS DOGWOOD'S `autoformalize-policies` SKILL PRINTS IT -- section 2b
// of ext/dogwood/.claude/skills/autoformalize-policies/SKILL.md, at c6237c88 -- verbatim below,
// deployed beside read access control so that a Read can actually be allowed or denied.
// Dogwood is (c) Amazon.com Inc, Apache 2.0. See README.md.
//
// Compare guide-set.dw: the same rule as the Dogwood guide and its gallery print it.

// -- ours: who may read. Anyone may read any document except the restricted one.
permit ( principal, action == Drupe::Action::"Read", resource );

forbid ( principal, action == Drupe::Action::"Read", resource )
when { context.input.document == "restricted" };

// -- the skill's example, verbatim
// Permit a Write only if this user read the same document within the last hour.
@id("write_after_read")
permit ( principal, action == Drupe::Action::"Write", resource )
when temporal {
    formerly within 1h Drupe::Action::"Read"::request{
        input.user: context.input.user,
        input.document: context.input.document
    }
};
